      "body": "densely_grouped_amines_interfere → uptake"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mechanism",
      "body": "buckled_staggered_ZnAtz_layers → uptake"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] use amine-functionalized Atz ligands to create amine-lined pores in a MOF → expected to improve low-pressure CO2 uptake by increasing heat-of-adsorption-driven binding"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] increase pore size and retain available amine groups in Zn-Atz frameworks by reducing the number of charge-balancing phosphate groups → larger amine-lined pores were anticipated and observed, with higher CO2 uptake expected"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "MOF 1 ({Zn3(Atz)3(PO4)}) vs MOF 2 ({Zn2(Atz)2(ox)}): winner=subject_a on pore_size"
    }
